 "briefing": "# Nvidia Briefing for 17 November 2026\n\n## Research Status\n\nNo verified changes at Nvidia for 16 October to 15 November 2026 were found. Every search returned an error, and no pages were fetched. This briefing therefore contains no claims about Nvidia's news, product launches, hires, or deals in that window. Before the meeting, the sources below should be checked directly.\n\n## Coverage by Category\n\n### News\n\nNo news items from the research window were verified. The Nvidia newsroom is the primary source for press releases and should be reviewed for any announcements dated 16 October to 15 November 2026: [Nvidia Newsroom](https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/). The Nvidia blog should also be checked for product and technology posts: [Nvidia Blog](https://blogs.nvidia.com/).\n\n### Product Launches\n\nNo product launches from the window were verified. Launch announcements are usually in the newsroom and blog above. Any launch referenced in the meeting should be confirmed against an official Nvidia page before it is discussed.\n\n### Executive and Notable Hires\n\nNo executive appointments, departures, or notable hires were verified. Officer changes are normally disclosed in SEC Form 8-K filings (Item 5.02). Nvidia's filing index should be reviewed: [SEC EDGAR, Nvidia filings](https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001045810). Executive profile updates may also be visible on LinkedIn, but none were reviewed.\n\n### Deals\n\nNo partnerships, acquisitions, investments, or supply or customer agreements were verified for the window. Material agreements would normally appear in newsroom releases or in 8-K Item 1.01 filings on the EDGAR index above. Investor materials, including the earnings calendar, are published here: [Nvidia Investor Relations](https://investor.nvidia.com/). The date of the next quarterly results release has not been confirmed and should be taken from that page.\n\n## Pre-Meeting Actions\n\n- Review the Nvidia newsroom and blog for the full window, 16 October to 15 November 2026.\n- Check the EDGAR 8-K index for filings dated in the window, with particular attention to Items 1.01, 5.02, and 8.01.\n- Confirm the next earnings date and any scheduled events on the investor relations site.\n- Check major financial and technology press for coverage of Nvidia in the window. Reuters and CNBC are listed below as starting points, but no articles from them were reviewed.\n\n## Open Questions for Nvidia\n\n1. Which announcements from 16 October to 15 November 2026 does Nvidia consider most material to our discussion, and where are the official releases or filings for them?\n2. Were any executive appointments, departures, or board changes made in this window, and how were they disclosed under SEC rules?\n3. Which partnerships, supply agreements, or investments signed in this window are expected to affect our relationship, and when will they be publicly disclosed?\n\n*Note: These questions are not grounded in verified changes because none were found. They should be revised once the primary sources above have been checked.*\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Nvidia Newsroom: https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/\n[2] Nvidia Blog: https://blogs.nvidia.com/\n[3] Nvidia Investor Relations: https://investor.nvidia.com/\n[4] SEC EDGAR, Nvidia filings: https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001045810\n[5] Reuters Technology: https://www.reuters.com/technology/\n[6] CNBC Nvidia: https://www.cnbc.com/nvidia/",
